package com.sliverzfx.gothicquest

data class Quest(
    val id: String,
    val chapter: Int,
    val playOrder: Int,
    val title: String,
    val aliases: List<String> = emptyList(),
    val category: String,
    val giver: String,
    val location: String,
    val prerequisites: String,
    val summary: String,
    val walkthroughSteps: List<String>,
    val reward: String,
    val warnings: String,
    val searchTags: List<String>
)

object GothicQuestData {
    val quests = listOf(
        Quest("G1-C1-01",1,1,"Admission to the Old Camp",listOf("Joining the Old Camp"),"Main / faction choice","Diego, Thorus, Gomez, Raven","Old Camp","Chapter I; not yet committed to another camp","Earn enough support among the Old Camp Shadows, complete Diego’s Test of Faith, then obtain Thorus’ permission to enter the castle and swear yourself to Gomez.",listOf("After Diego introduces the Old Camp, ask how you can become one of them. Thorus sends you back to Diego for the formal test and tells you that the Shadows’ opinion matters.","Complete Test of Faith by obtaining Ian’s list from the Old Mine. If you also want the New Camp option, let Lares alter the list before returning it to Diego; Diego can still accept it.","Build support with Old Camp Shadows. The most useful tracked jobs are Vanished Guard, Recipe of the Sect and New Fence for Fisk. Snaf, Fingers, Scatty and Whistler can also improve your standing through their smaller tasks or tests.","When Diego is satisfied, tell Thorus that you have Diego’s approval. Enter the inner castle and speak with Gomez. Answer respectfully and avoid claiming useful contacts you cannot back up.","After Gomez accepts you, speak with Raven to receive your Shadow armor and continue the main story."),"Shadow status, Shadow Garb; admission XP from supporting tasks","Joining any major camp advances the story and closes the other two admission paths. Make a permanent save before committing if you want to experience all three routes.",listOf("old camp","admission","shadow","diego","thorus","gomez")),
        Quest("G1-C1-02",1,2,"Test of Faith",listOf("Trial of Trust"),"Old Camp / admission","Diego","Old Camp → Old Mine","Ask Diego about joining the Old Camp after speaking with Thorus","Retrieve Ian’s supply list from the Old Mine and bring it back to Diego; optionally let Lares forge it first.",listOf("Ask Diego exactly why Ian should give the list to you. This dialogue matters: without Diego’s explanation, Ian may refuse and force a second trip.","If needed, get a map from Graham near the Old Camp north gate. He asks for ore, but intimidation can also get the map.","Travel to the Old Mine, descend the wooden walkways and find Ian near the populated work area. Tell him Diego sent you and take the list.","Optional: before returning to Diego, take the list to Lares in the New Camp. He adds extra requirements so the New Camp can profit from or ambush the shipment.","Return the list to Diego. If Lares altered it, go back to Lares afterward for his follow-up reward and speak with Gorn when directed."),"750 XP for delivery to Diego; additional New Camp rewards possible","Giving Lares the list does not prevent Old Camp admission. It is one of the best early actions if you want to keep both Old and New Camp choices open.",listOf("test of faith","old mine","ian","supply list","diego")),
        Quest("G1-C1-03",1,3,"Snaf's Recipe",category="Old Camp / side quest",giver="Snaf",location="Old Camp → south-gate cave",prerequisites="Speak with Snaf",summary="Collect hell mushrooms and meatbug meat so Snaf can cook his specialty.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Snaf asks for 8 hell mushrooms and 3 portions of meatbug meat.","Leave the Old Camp through the south gate. Search the nearby cave/rocky area for the mushrooms.","Kill meatbugs around the ruined huts and collect three pieces of meatbug meat.","Return all ingredients to Snaf.","Afterward, Snaf can provide portions of his meatbug stew on a recurring basis."),reward="100 XP; recurring meatbug stew; Old Camp admission support",warnings="Excellent to combine with Vanished Guard because both objectives are in the same south-gate area.",searchTags=listOf("snaf","meatbug","hell mushroom","recipe")),
        Quest("G1-C1-04",1,4,"Vanished Guard",listOf("The Missing Guardsman"),"Old Camp / side quest","Sly","Old Camp","Speak to Sly in the outer ring","Find the missing guard Nek and return his amulet to Sly.",listOf("Sly asks you to find Nek. Talk with Fletcher and other guards if you want clues, then ask Snaf; the cook mentions the mushrooms/meatbug area outside the south gate.","Leave through the south gate and search the small cave in the rock wall not far from the path. Clear the molerats if necessary.","Inside you will find Nek’s corpse. Loot Nek’s Amulet.","Return to Sly and hand over the amulet to close the quest."),"250 XP","This quest helps your Old Camp admission and is easiest to combine with Snaf’s Recipe because both send you outside the south gate.",listOf("nek","sly","missing guard","old camp")),
        Quest("G1-C1-05",1,5,"Thorus' Quest",listOf("Thorus' Assignment"),"Old Camp / admission","Thorus","Old Camp","Ask about working for Gomez","Remove Mordrag from the Old Camp without creating problems for Thorus.",listOf("Find Mordrag near the Old Camp south gate and confront him about Thorus’ order.","The safest all-purpose solution is to agree to go with Mordrag to the New Camp. Follow him there; the job is considered handled and you gain a valuable introduction to Lares’ faction.","Alternatively, defeat Mordrag in a non-lethal duel and tell him to leave. This route is required if you want New Fence for Fisk.","Killing Mordrag permanently also satisfies Thorus, but it destroys an important route into the New Camp and removes later interactions.","Return to Thorus after Mordrag has been removed by your chosen method."),"Varies by solution; Mordrag escort grants his ring/connection","For a completionist playthrough, escorting Mordrag preserves the most content. For New Fence for Fisk specifically, knock him out rather than escorting or killing him.",listOf("thorus","mordrag","old camp","new camp")),
        Quest("G1-C1-06",1,6,"New Fence for Fisk",category="Old Camp / side quest",giver="Fisk",location="Old Camp → New Camp",prerequisites="Defeat Mordrag non-lethally during Thorus’ Quest",summary="Find Fisk a new supplier after Mordrag is driven from the Old Camp.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("After knocking Mordrag out and ordering him to leave, speak with Fisk. He complains that losing Mordrag also means losing his fence/supplier.","Travel to the New Camp and find Sharky, a merchant in the camp’s cave system.","Tell Sharky about Fisk’s business opportunity and persuade him to take over the arrangement.","Return to Fisk in the Old Camp and report that Sharky will work with him."),reward="300 XP; Old Camp admission support",warnings="This quest only appears from the non-lethal “drive Mordrag away” solution. Escorting Mordrag to the New Camp or killing him will not produce the same setup.",searchTags=listOf("fisk","sharky","fence","mordrag")),
        Quest("G1-C1-07",1,7,"Recipe of the Sect",category="Old Camp / side quest",giver="Dexter",location="Old Camp → Swamp Camp",prerequisites="Speak with Dexter",summary="Steal Cor Kalom’s swampweed recipe for Dexter.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Accept Dexter’s job and negotiate for an advance if you want some ore up front.","Travel to the Swamp Camp and enter Cor Kalom’s laboratory area. Wait for a safe moment if NPCs are watching.","Open the relevant chest in the laboratory. A commonly documented lock combination is Right, Right, Left, Right.","Take the recipe and return to Dexter in the Old Camp.","Hand it over to complete the job and improve your standing for Old Camp admission."),reward="350 XP; Old Camp admission support; ore advance can be negotiated",warnings="Save before stealing. NPC awareness and lockpicking can make the theft messy if you are caught.",searchTags=listOf("dexter","cor kalom","recipe","theft","lockpick")),
        Quest("G1-C1-08",1,8,"Admission to the New Camp",listOf("Joining the New Camp"),"Main / faction choice","Lares","New Camp","Chapter I; not yet committed to another camp","Prove to Lares that you can help the New Camp by bringing useful information, contacts and ore-producing opportunities.",listOf("Reach the New Camp, preferably by allowing Mordrag to escort you from the Old Camp. His introduction is useful and keeps relations friendly.","Speak with Lares in the upper cave. The admission system is flexible: several actions count toward his confidence, and you only need enough of them to pass.","The strongest route is to complete Canvassing of Customers / The Weed Merchant business around the camp, then bring Ian’s Old Mine supply list to Lares before returning it to Diego. Lares alters the list and plans to exploit the Old Camp shipment.","Handle Roscoe correctly the first time you enter Lares’ area and make use of Mordrag’s connection; these are easy admission opportunities to miss if you rush the dialogue.","Return to Lares after you have done enough. He accepts you as a bandit and gives access to the New Camp progression."),"Bandit status, Light Bandit Clothing; XP from admission objectives","You can still finish Test of Faith for Diego after letting Lares alter the list. Do not kill Mordrag during Thorus’ Quest if you intend to use the New Camp route.",listOf("new camp","admission","bandit","lares","mordrag","supply list")),
        Quest("G1-C1-09",1,9,"Water Carrier for Lefty",category="New Camp / side quest",giver="Lefty",location="New Camp rice fields",prerequisites="Enter the rice fields",summary="Distribute water to the rice-field workers, then stand up to Lefty when he tries to make the job permanent.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Lefty stops you in the rice fields and orders you to distribute water to the farmers.","Get the water supply from the Rice Lord and hand water to the ten field workers Lefty expects you to serve.","Return to Lefty after the first round. He tries to turn the favor into a daily obligation.","Refuse. Defeat Lefty in a non-lethal fight; depending on how the scene develops, the Rice Lord can also become involved.","After winning, tell Lefty he can carry the water himself. The farmers’ forced service is no longer your responsibility."),reward="400 XP; freedom from Lefty’s forced chore",warnings="Do not kill named NPCs unless you deliberately want to cut content. A knockout is enough.",searchTags=listOf("lefty","rice lord","water carrier","rice fields")),
        Quest("G1-C1-10",1,10,"Horatio the Peasant",listOf("Horatio"),"New Camp / side quest","Horatio","New Camp rice fields","Speak to Horatio; learn his history from Jeremiah","Convince Horatio that you oppose the Rice Lord so he will teach you his strength technique.",listOf("Find Horatio working in the rice fields and ask about his situation. He will not immediately share his technique.","Go to the New Camp tavern and speak with Jeremiah. Learn about Horatio’s grudge against the Rice Lord.","Return to Horatio and make it clear that you want the strength to stand against the Rice Lord, not to bully weaker people.","Horatio teaches you, granting a permanent Strength increase."),"Permanent +5 Strength; no separate XP in some guides","Because the reward is a direct stat increase, min-max players may prefer to use it after buying normal Strength training near the trainer cap so the free bonus pushes above it.",listOf("horatio","strength","rice lord","permanent bonus")),
        Quest("G1-C1-11",1,11,"Lurker at the Dam",category="New Camp / side quest",giver="Homer",location="New Camp dam",prerequisites="Speak with Homer",summary="Kill the lurker damaging the New Camp dam.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Talk with Homer, the man responsible for the dam. He explains that a lurker is causing trouble below it.","Go down to the shoreline beneath/near the dam and search the water’s edge.","Kill the Dam Lurker. Be careful around the water because melee positioning can be awkward.","Return to Homer and report the kill."),reward="300 XP",warnings="A simple early quest, but the creature can be dangerous at very low level. Pull it onto open ground if needed.",searchTags=listOf("homer","dam","lurker","new camp")),
        Quest("G1-C1-12",1,12,"Canvassing of Customers",listOf("Customer Recruitment"),"New Camp / side quest","Baal Kagan","New Camp","Speak with Baal Kagan","Sell Kagan’s Green Novice swampweed to New Camp residents and return for your reward.",listOf("Baal Kagan gives you 10 Green Novice stalks to distribute in the New Camp.","Sell or hand one stalk to ten different suitable customers. Spread them around rather than trying to sell the full stack to one person.","Return to Kagan when all ten are gone.","Choose your reward. If you are pursuing Swamp Camp admission, take the specially prepared Dreamcall and save it for Baal Tyon."),"200 XP; choice of ore, scrolls, or prepared Dreamcall","The reward choice matters. The prepared Dreamcall is effectively an admission tool for the Brotherhood, while ore or scrolls are short-term rewards.",listOf("kagan","green novice","swampweed","customers","baal tyon")),
        Quest("G1-C1-13",1,13,"The Weed Merchant",listOf("The Herb Merchant"),"New Camp / side quest","Baal Kagan / Isidro","New Camp tavern","Progress Kagan’s work and meet Lares","Take over Isidro’s swampweed sales and settle the proceeds.",listOf("After dealing with Kagan, find Isidro in Silas’ tavern. He has been neglecting his job and is willing to let you handle his weed.","Take Isidro’s stock and sell it around the New Camp until you have converted it into ore.","Lares is interested in the business and can receive the proceeds as part of proving your usefulness to the New Camp.","Make sure Isidro receives the share needed to settle his side of the arrangement; if necessary, pay him from your own ore after dealing with Lares.","Return to the relevant NPCs and exhaust the follow-up dialogue to close the task."),"About 500 XP; ore handling depends on route","Because the ore can be routed in different ways, save before final turn-ins if you want to optimize both Lares’ admission credit and Isidro’s outcome.",listOf("isidro","weed merchant","lares","swampweed","new camp")),
        Quest("G1-C1-14",1,14,"Shrike's Hut",category="New Camp / side quest",giver="Gorn",location="New Camp",prerequisites="Speak with Gorn",summary="Convince Shrike to leave the hut Gorn wants cleared.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Gorn tells you that Shrike has occupied a hut and needs to be removed.","Find Shrike at the hut and demand that he leave.","When he refuses, defeat him in a non-lethal fight.","Speak to Shrike after the fight and make him move out.","Report success to Gorn."),reward="300 XP; access to the hut",warnings="Knock Shrike out rather than killing him; the quest is designed around intimidation.",searchTags=listOf("gorn","shrike","hut","new camp")),
        Quest("G1-C1-15",1,15,"Baloro's Weapon",listOf("Baloros Weapon"),"New Camp / side quest","Baloro","Free Mine / New Camp territory","Reach Baloro near the Free Mine","Collect Baloro’s long shopping list in exchange for a weapon he ultimately does not give you.",listOf("Baloro promises a powerful weapon if you bring him supplies.","Collect 5 apples, 2 rice schnapps, 5 beers, 3 loaves of bread, 2 cheeses and 2 grapes. Most can be bought or looted while doing other Chapter I errands.","Return to Baloro with the full list.","Hand over the provisions. He admits there is no special weapon and the quest ends with experience instead."),"250 XP; no promised weapon","The “weapon” is a scam; do not overspend scarce ore just to rush this quest unless you value the experience.",listOf("baloro","weapon","provisions","free mine")),
        Quest("G1-C1-16",1,16,"Admission to the Swamp Camp",listOf("Joining the Swamp Camp"),"Main / faction choice","Cor Kalom and the Baals","Swamp Camp","Chapter I; not yet committed to another camp","Win the approval of at least four influential Baals, then report to Cor Kalom and become a novice of the Brotherhood.",listOf("Talk to Lester and the camp members to learn that the Baals only listen when you demonstrate faith or usefulness rather than simply asking for a vote.","Baal Namib: coordinate with Lester and perform the staged “conversion” conversation so Namib believes you have accepted the Sleeper’s teachings.","Baal Tyon: during Canvassing of Customers in the New Camp, choose the specially prepared Dreamcall as Baal Kagan’s reward and give it to Tyon.","Baal Orun: complete Ghorim’s Replacement, then The Swampweed Harvest and deliver the harvest as instructed.","Baal Cadar: obtain a Sleep scroll and use it on one of his students while Cadar is watching. Baal Tondral: complete New Souls for the Brotherhood by bringing Dusty to the camp.","Once four Baals support you, return to Cor Kalom. You are admitted as a novice and Chapter II can begin."),"Novice status, Novice Robe; substantial XP from guru approval chains","You do not need every Baal. Choosing the prepared Dreamcall from Kagan is the cleanest way to secure Tyon’s vote, so do not spend that reward choice casually if you want this faction.",listOf("swamp camp","brotherhood","novice","baal","cor kalom")),
        Quest("G1-C1-17",1,17,"Ghorim's Replacement",listOf("Relief for Ghorim"),"Swamp Camp / admission","Ghorim / Baal Orun","Swamp Camp presses","Speak to Ghorim and observe Harlok’s absence","Force Harlok to take over his shift so Ghorim can finally rest.",listOf("Talk to Ghorim at the swampweed presses. His replacement Harlok has not shown up.","Find Harlok elsewhere in the camp and tell him to relieve Ghorim.","Harlok refuses; defeat him in a non-lethal fight.","After he gets back up, speak to him again and order him to take the shift.","Return to Ghorim, then speak with Baal Orun. Orun now trusts you with the swampweed harvest task."),"400 XP; unlocks The Swampweed Harvest / Orun approval chain","Do not kill Harlok. The follow-up conversation after the knockout is what advances the quest.",listOf("ghorim","harlok","baal orun","swampweed")),
        Quest("G1-C1-18",1,18,"The Swampweed Harvest",category="Swamp Camp / admission",giver="Baal Orun",location="Swamp Camp",prerequisites="Complete Ghorim’s Replacement",summary="Collect both harvesting groups’ swampweed and deliver the full load to Cor Kalom.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("After Ghorim’s Replacement, speak with Baal Orun. He sends you to collect the harvest from the swamp workers.","Visit Balor’s group and receive their 50 swampweed plants.","Find Viran’s group deeper in the swamp. Kill the bloodflies around his workers, including the ones near the small island, so the harvest can be completed; receive another 50.","Deliver all 100 plants to Cor Kalom in his laboratory.","Return to Baal Orun for completion and his approval. The reward chain can provide a Sleep scroll, useful for Baal Cadar’s test."),reward="About 1,150 XP across the chain; Sleep scroll; Baal Orun approval",warnings="Keep the Sleep scroll if you are working on Admission to the Swamp Camp; it can secure another Baal vote immediately.",searchTags=listOf("swampweed harvest","balor","viran","cor kalom","baal orun")),
        Quest("G1-C1-19",1,19,"New Souls for the Brotherhood",category="Swamp Camp / admission",giver="Baal Tondral / Dusty",location="Swamp Camp ↔ Old Camp",prerequisites="Speak with Baal Tondral; find Dusty in the Old Camp",summary="Help Dusty leave the Old Camp and join the Brotherhood.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Baal Tondral wants you to bring a new believer to the camp. In the Old Camp, find Dusty and talk about the Brotherhood.","Visit Melvin in the Swamp Camp if needed and carry his message/information back to Dusty; this helps convince Dusty that leaving is possible.","Dusty agrees to come, but the Old Camp south gate guards expect a payment. Pay the 100 ore bribe to get him out without a fight.","Escort Dusty safely along the road to the Swamp Camp.","Bring him to Baal Tondral and report success."),reward="500 XP; Baal Tondral approval",warnings="Keep Dusty close on the road; clear dangerous creatures first if your route is not already safe.",searchTags=listOf("dusty","baal tondral","brotherhood","escort")),
        Quest("G1-C1-20",1,20,"Aaron's Chest",category="Old Mine / side quest",giver="Snipes",location="Old Mine",prerequisites="Meet Snipes and Aaron",summary="Trick Aaron away from his chest, buy the key from Snipes and loot it.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Snipes points out Aaron’s locked chest and proposes getting Aaron out of the way.","Tell Aaron that Ian wants to see him. Aaron leaves his post.","Return to Snipes and buy the chest key; the documented price is 30 ore.","Open Aaron’s chest and take the contents.","Optional: later sell the key back to Aaron for a small amount of ore once the chest is already empty."),reward="150 XP; chest loot; optional ore from reselling the key",warnings="The scheme is more profitable if you loot the chest before Aaron returns. Save if you are experimenting with dialogue order.",searchTags=listOf("aaron","snipes","chest","old mine")),
        Quest("G1-C1-21",1,21,"Ulbert's Storeshed",listOf("Ulbert's Storage"),"Old Mine / side quest","Ulbert / Aleph","Old Mine","Reach the mine storage area","Distract Ulbert and use the stolen storeshed key to empty the storage room.",listOf("Talk to Ulbert. Give him a drink to loosen his tongue and learn that his key was stolen.","Find Aleph and buy the stolen key. A commonly documented price is 30 ore; it can rise if you previously informed on Aleph.","Return to Ulbert and lure him away by claiming Ian has roast meat for him.","Use the key to enter and loot the storeshed while Ulbert is gone.","When Ulbert later confronts you, dismiss the accusation to finish the interaction."),"75 XP plus storeroom loot","If you intend to exploit Aleph’s other deals, avoid antagonizing him before buying the key.",listOf("ulbert","aleph","storeshed","old mine")),
        Quest("G1-C1-22",1,22,"The Big Thing of the Brotherhood",listOf("The Brotherhood’s Great Plan (Old Camp)"),"Old Camp / faction report","Raven","Old Camp → Swamp Camp","Join Old Camp and progress Brotherhood storyline","Find out what the Brotherhood is planning and report it to Raven.",listOf("After joining the Old Camp, Raven asks you to investigate the Brotherhood’s activities.","Continue the Swamp Camp main story: obtain the focus for Y’Berion and help Cor Kalom acquire the minecrawler secretion/eggs.","Once the Brotherhood’s plan for the Great Invocation/Calling becomes clear, return to Raven.","Report what you learned to close the Old Camp version of this faction quest."),"Story/faction progression; no separate XP in some guides","This is one of two mutually exclusive versions of the same journal concept. The New Camp has its own report-to-Lares version.",listOf("brotherhood","raven","old camp","great calling")),
        Quest("G1-C1-23",1,23,"The Big Thing of the Brotherhood",listOf("The Brotherhood’s Great Plan (New Camp)"),"New Camp / faction report","Lares","New Camp → Swamp Camp","Join New Camp and progress Brotherhood storyline","Learn what the Brotherhood’s Great Calling is meant to accomplish and report it to Lares.",listOf("After joining the New Camp, ask Lares about work. He wants intelligence on the Brotherhood’s plans.","Continue the Swamp Camp story far enough to learn about the Great Calling, including the focus and minecrawler-secretion preparations.","Once the purpose of the Brotherhood’s ritual is clear, return to Lares.","Report your findings to complete the New Camp version of the quest."),"Story/faction progression; no separate XP in some guides","Mutually exclusive with Raven’s Old Camp version in a normal playthrough.",listOf("brotherhood","lares","new camp","great calling")),
        Quest("G1-C1-24",1,24,"The Stranger",category="Secret / exploration quest",giver="Trigger quest",location="Sunken Tower and Colony-wide locations",prerequisites="Defeat the Skeleton Mage and read Chromanin",summary="Follow six cryptic Chromanin clues across the Colony to complete Gothic’s hidden treasure hunt.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Defeat the Skeleton Mage in/near the Sunken Tower and read the first Chromanin book found on his body. This activates the chain.","Chromanin II is on top of the old castle/fortress. A Transform into Meatbug scroll is a practical way to reach confined areas involved in this hunt.","Chromanin III is on the small island in the river north of the Old Camp approach.","Chromanin IV lies near the ruined huts on the lake shore by the New Camp; Chromanin V is on the shore near the Sunken Tower.","Return to the place where the Skeleton Mage died for Chromanin VI and the conclusion."),reward="About 3,350 XP total",warnings="This is a late-game-strength secret despite being listed with Chapter I content in some catalogs. Do not assume it is meant for a fresh level-one character.",searchTags=listOf("chromanin","stranger","secret","sunken tower")),
        // Chapter II — The Nest of the Minecrawlers
        Quest("G1-C2-01",2,1,"Focus for the Gurus",listOf("A Focus for the Gurus"),"Main","Y’Berion","Swamp Camp → western cliff area","Join any camp; speak with Brotherhood leadership","Recover the stolen focus stone from Nyras and bring it to Y’Berion.",listOf("After joining a camp, go to the Swamp Camp. Lester directs you to Y’Berion, who explains that a novice named Nyras was sent for a focus stone and never returned.","Take the map/directions and travel to the marked western cliff area.","Find Nyras. The focus has affected him and he attacks rather than returning peacefully.","Defeat Nyras and loot the focus stone from him.","Return to Y’Berion. The recovered focus moves the Brotherhood’s Great Calling preparations forward."),"1,000 XP; story progression","Nyras must be defeated; there is no peaceful completion path.",listOf("nyras","focus","yberion","gurus")),
        Quest("G1-C2-02",2,2,"Taking Weeds to Gomez",listOf("The Weed Delivery"),"Swamp Camp / faction quest","Cor Kalom / Bartholo","Swamp Camp → Old Camp castle","Join Swamp Camp as a novice","Deliver the Brotherhood’s swampweed shipment to the Old Camp.",listOf("As a Brotherhood novice, accept Cor Kalom’s delivery job and take the 30 Dreamcall stalks.","Travel to the Old Camp and enter the castle. Your faction membership gives you the access needed.","Find Bartholo and hand over the shipment.","Collect the 500 ore payment.","Return to Cor Kalom and give him the proceeds."),"400 XP; 500 ore is collected for Cor Kalom","If this and The Weed Monopoly are active together, save before turn-ins. Old Gothic scripts/localizations can be finicky when the two weed jobs are reported in an unusual order.",listOf("weed delivery","gomez","bartholo","cor kalom","dreamcall")),
        Quest("G1-C2-03",2,3,"Secretion of the Minecrawlers",listOf("Secret of the Minecrawlers"),"Main","Cor Kalom","Swamp Camp → Old Mine","Complete Focus for the Gurus","Open the sealed minecrawler nest, kill the queen and bring its eggs/secretion to Cor Kalom.",listOf("Cor Kalom needs powerful minecrawler secretion for the ritual and sends you to the Old Mine.","Speak with Ian. Before he can help open the deeper gate, recover the missing gearwheel from a side tunnel guarded by minecrawlers.","Bring the gearwheel to Ian, learn the gate procedure/password and speak with Asghan at the sealed minecrawler gate.","Recruit two or three templars to help. Gor-Na-Bar, Gor-Na-Kosh and Gor-Na-Vid are common candidates; one may require a healing potion before he can assist.","Open the gate, clear the nest and kill the Minecrawler Queen. Loot the queen’s eggs/secretion.","Return to Cor Kalom and hand over what he needs for the Great Calling."),"Large XP reward (about 5,500 in detailed walkthroughs); Light rune or potion reward option","Search the queen’s chamber thoroughly before leaving. The Old Mine becomes inaccessible later in the story.",listOf("minecrawler queen","old mine","cor kalom","gearwheel")),
        Quest("G1-C2-04",2,4,"The Weed Monopoly",category="Swamp Camp / faction quest",giver="Cor Kalom",location="Cave southeast of New Camp",prerequisites="Join Swamp Camp as a novice",summary="Shut down the independent swampweed operation competing with the Brotherhood.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Cor Kalom tells you about illegal producers selling swampweed outside Brotherhood control.","Travel to the cave southeast of the New Camp and confront Jacko and his associates.","The cleanest solution is intimidation: make it clear that the templars will deal with them if they continue. A bribe/silence route may also be available depending on dialogue.","Avoid simply murdering everyone if you want reliable journal completion; combat-first solutions can leave the quest state awkward in some versions.","Return to Cor Kalom and report that the operation has been stopped."),reward="About 1,250 XP",warnings="Use a manual save before the confrontation and another before reporting to Kalom, especially if Taking Weeds to Gomez is also active.",searchTags=listOf("weed monopoly","jacko","swamp camp","cor kalom")),
        Quest("G1-C2-05",2,5,"Almanac",category="Main",giver="Cor Kalom / Talas",location="Swamp Camp → Goblin Cave",prerequisites="Progress the Great Calling preparations",summary="Recover the Brotherhood’s stolen Almanac from goblins.",walkthroughSteps=listOf("Cor Kalom explains that the Almanac needed for the ritual has been stolen.","Talas can guide you toward the goblin cave. Follow him to the area, then continue inside yourself.","Clear the goblins and search the right-hand passages/tunnel system.","Find the chest containing the Almanac and take it.","Return to Cor Kalom with the book."),reward="About 2,500 XP",warnings="Bring enough healing and avoid getting surrounded in the narrow cave passages.",searchTags=listOf("almanac","talas","goblin cave","cor kalom")),
        Quest("G1-C3-01",3,1,"Orc Cemetery",listOf("The Orc Cemetery"),"Main","Cor Angar / Baal Lukor","Swamp Camp → Orc Cemetery","Great Calling has failed","Investigate the Orc Cemetery with Baal Lukor and discover why the Sleeper did not answer the Brotherhood.",listOf("After the failed ritual, Cor Angar sends you to investigate the Orc Cemetery. Talas can lead you to the entrance.","Enter the cemetery and find Baal Lukor. Keep him alive while clearing the first chambers.","Explore the three main corridors. In the right and central routes, recover the two halves of an orcish scroll; use switches where necessary and let Lukor interpret the text.","In the left route, use the orc teleport spell/scroll to pass the sealed wall, operate the winch and open the deeper path.","Reach the hidden chamber. The expected revelation is absent, and Lukor eventually turns hostile. Defeat him.","Return to Cor Angar and report the failure."),"","",listOf("orc cemetery","baal lukor","cor angar","talas")),
        Quest("G1-C3-02",3,2,"Medicinal Herbs for Y'Berion",listOf("Healing Herbs for Y'Berion"),"Main","Cor Angar","Swamp Camp","Return from Orc Cemetery","Gather the strongest healing herbs for the dying Y’Berion.",listOf("Cor Angar tells you that Y’Berion is gravely ill and asks for five of the strongest healing herbs.","Search the swamp for the distinctive high-grade healing plants, especially around the water and vegetation away from the main walkways.","If you cannot find enough, repeatedly ask Cor Angar about the missing supply; in some routes Fortuno can provide the required five plants.","Bring five strong healing herbs back to Cor Angar/Y’Berion.","The story continues regardless: Y’Berion’s condition reveals that the Brotherhood must abandon its original plan."),"1,500 XP; story progression","",listOf("yberion","medicinal herbs","cor angar","fortuno")),
        Quest("G1-C3-03",3,3,"Escape Plan of the New Camp",listOf("The New Camp's Escape Plan"),"Main","Cor Angar → Saturas","Swamp Camp → New Camp","Y’Berion dies / Brotherhood plan collapses","Carry Y’Berion’s final evidence to the Water Mages so they can attempt their own escape plan.",listOf("After Y’Berion’s death, speak with Cor Angar. He gives you access to Cor Kalom’s chest and explains that the focus and Almanac should go to the Water Mages.","Open Kalom’s chest and take the Almanac and the relevant focus stone.","Travel to the New Camp. Gorn helps direct you toward the Water Mages; Cronos guards access to their area.","Use the password/countersign TETRIANDOCH when required and enter the Water Mages’ section.","Give Saturas the Almanac and focus. He explains the New Camp’s plan and begins the search for the remaining focus stones."),"1,500 XP","",listOf("escape plan","saturas","water mages","almanac","focus")),
        Quest("G1-C3-04",3,4,"Search for the Focus Stones",listOf(),"Main / hub quest","Saturas","New Camp","Complete Escape Plan of the New Camp","Recover the four remaining focus stones scattered around the Colony.",listOf("After receiving the Almanac and first focus, Saturas gives you a map and sends you after the four remaining stones.","Speak with Riordian and the other Water Mages for supplies and information before leaving.","Complete the four focus quests in any order: Ring of Stone, Mountain Fort, Monastery Ruins and Troll Canyon.","After each recovery, return to Saturas. Reporting them individually is convenient and can unlock additional supplies or dialogue.","When all four have been returned, the Water Mages are ready for the next stage: seeking aid from the Fire Mages."),"Story progression; each focus subquest gives major XP; Water Mage teleport utility","",listOf("focus stones","saturas","water mages","map")),
        Quest("G1-C3-05",3,5,"Focus in the Troll Canyon",listOf(),"Main / focus stone","Diego","Troll Canyon","Search for the Focus Stones","Shrink the canyon troll, let Diego repair the winch and recover the focus beyond the gate.",listOf("Find Diego near Troll Canyon and follow his explanation of the blocked route.","Locate the Shrink Monster scroll in the area before engaging the troll.","Cast Shrink Monster on the troll, then kill the miniaturized creature.","Diego repairs/operates the jammed winch so the gate can be opened.","Pass through, defeat the harpies in the ruins and take the focus stone. Return it to Saturas."),"About 3,500 XP; bonus if returned last","",listOf("troll canyon","diego","shrink monster","focus")),
        Quest("G1-C3-06",3,6,"Focus in the Mountain Fort",listOf("Focus in the Mountain Fortress"),"Main / focus stone","Lester","Mountain Fort","Search for the Focus Stones","Use Lester’s telekinesis solution to retrieve the inaccessible focus stone.",listOf("Meet Lester near the bridge leading into the ruined Mountain Fort and clear the dangerous approach.","Explore the fort and find the library. A chest there contains the key/item needed to progress upward.","In the upper area, recover the old deed/document Lester is interested in and give it to him.","Lester rewards/helpfully provides a Telekinesis scroll.","Use Telekinesis to pull the focus stone from the otherwise unreachable platform, then return it to Saturas."),"About 3,500 XP; bonus if returned last","",listOf("mountain fort","lester","telekinesis","focus")),
        Quest("G1-C3-07",3,7,"Focus under the Ring of Stone",listOf("Focus Under the Stonehenge"),"Main / focus stone","Milten","Ring of Stone / Stonehenge crypt","Search for the Focus Stones","Recover the focus from the crypt beneath the stone circle with Milten’s help.",listOf("Find Milten near the Ring of Stone. He gives you a Destroy Undead spell to deal with the crypt guardian.","Enter the underground crypt. If possible, lure ordinary skeletons away and destroy them before confronting the stronger warden.","Use Destroy Undead on the key undead target when you have a clear cast.","Loot the crypt key and the orcish talisman; give the talisman to Milten if the dialogue is available.","Open the chest containing the focus stone and return it to Saturas."),"About 3,500 XP; bonus if returned last; Orcish talisman side reward","",listOf("ring of stone","stonehenge","milten","focus","undead")),
        Quest("G1-C3-08",3,8,"Focus in the Monastery Ruins",listOf("Focus in the Monastery Ruin"),"Main / focus stone","Gorn","Monastery Ruins","Search for the Focus Stones","Enter the sealed monastery ruins, defeat the creatures inside and recover the focus.",listOf("Meet Gorn near the ruined monastery and clear the immediate threats.","Search the side cave for a Transform into Meatbug scroll. Use the tiny form to crawl through the gap beneath the closed gate.","Inside, return to normal form and operate the winch to open the gate for Gorn.","Explore the ruins, defeat the shadowbeast and search the chest holding the focus stone.","Watch for the young troll outside/near the ruins on the way out. Return the focus to Saturas."),"About 3,500 XP; bonus if returned last","",listOf("monastery ruins","gorn","meatbug","focus","shadowbeast")),
        Quest("G1-C3-09",3,9,"Aid of the Magicians of Fire",listOf("Help of the Fire Mages"),"Main","Saturas","New Camp → Old Camp","Return all focus stones","Ask the Fire Mages to help the Water Mages, only to discover that Gomez has already murdered them.",listOf("After all focus stones are returned, Saturas asks you to seek the Fire Mages’ cooperation and gives you a teleport rune/means to reach them.","Travel toward the Old Camp. The situation has changed dramatically after the collapse of the Old Mine.","Near the camp, Diego and/or Milten warn you that Gomez has seized power, attacked the Free Mine and had the Fire Mages killed.","Do not try to walk through hostile guards as if nothing changed. Use safe routes and speak with the surviving friends outside.","Return to Saturas and report that the Fire Mages cannot help."),"About 1,000 XP; triggers the Old Camp crisis","",listOf("fire mages","saturas","old camp","gomez","chapter 4")),
        Quest("G1-C3-10",3,10,"Banishment from the Old Camp",listOf("Exile from the Old Camp"),"Main / faction transition","Fletcher / Bloodwyn / Saturas","Old Camp outskirts → New Camp","Aid of the Magicians of Fire / Old Mine collapse","Survive Gomez’s purge and formally sever your connection to the Old Camp.",listOf("After the Old Mine collapses and Gomez attacks the Free Mine, approaching the Old Camp reveals that former allies such as guards are now hostile.","Speak with Diego/Milten outside to understand what happened and avoid forcing your way through the camp.","Return to Saturas and report the situation as part of the Water Mages’ new plan.","If you were a Fire Mage, the story can transition you toward the Water Mages. If you were a Guard, Lee can accept you among the Mercenaries after the appropriate dialogue."),"Faction change for former Fire Mage/Guard paths; no separate XP in some guides","",listOf("banishment","exile","old camp","gomez","faction transition")),
        Quest("G1-C4-01",4,1,"The Meeting",listOf(),"Side / friends","Diego","Outside Old Camp south gate","Old Camp crisis","Pass Diego’s message to Gorn and Lester so the four friends can coordinate.",listOf("Find Diego near the southern side of the Old Camp after the camp becomes hostile.","He asks you to tell Gorn and Lester about a meeting.","Find Gorn in/near the New Camp, commonly around Saturas during this story phase, and deliver Diego’s message.","Find Lester in the Mountain Fort library area and inform him as well.","Return to Diego to report that both have been contacted."),"About 2,000 XP","",listOf("meeting","diego","gorn","lester","four friends")),
        Quest("G1-C4-02",4,2,"Xardas the Necromancer",listOf(),"Main","Saturas / Demon servant","Xardas’ tower","Aid of the Magicians of Fire","Reach Xardas by defeating his three elemental golems and earning access to his tower.",listOf("Saturas directs you to the outcast necromancer Xardas, whose tower lies in dangerous territory.","Near the tower, study the Arcanum Golum notes/books if available; each guardian has a specific weakness.","Defeat the Stone Golem with blunt damage, the Ice Golem with fire, and the Fire Golem with ice/lightning-type magic. Loot each golem’s heart.","Enter the tower and present the three hearts to Xardas’ demon servant/lord as proof.","Use the teleport access provided to reach Xardas himself and speak with him about the Sleeper."),"About 5,000 XP; access to Xardas and teleport utility","",listOf("xardas","golems","necromancer","golem hearts")),
        Quest("G1-C4-03",4,3,"The Banished Orc Shaman",listOf("The Exiled Orc Shaman"),"Main","Xardas / Ur-Shak","Old castle east of main routes","Speak with Xardas","Find the exiled shaman Ur-Shak and learn the truth about the Sleeper and the underground temple.",listOf("Xardas tells you that an exiled orc shaman may know more about the Sleeper.","Travel to the ruined old castle/fortress area east of the central Colony routes.","Find Ur-Shak under attack by temple warriors and help him survive the fight.","Speak with Ur-Shak afterward. He explains the Sleeper’s origins and the existence of the temple beneath the Orc City.","Accept the Orcish Talisman he gives you and return to Xardas with the information."),"About 2,000 XP; Orcish Talisman (+fire resistance); lore progression","",listOf("ur-shak","orc shaman","xardas","sleeper")),
        Quest("G1-C4-04",4,4,"Minecrawler's Plate Armor",listOf("Minecrawler Plate Armor"),"Side / equipment","Wolf","New Camp → Free Mine","Chapter IV; speak with Gorn/Wolf around Free Mine retaking","Collect 15 minecrawler plates so Wolf can build a unique heavy armor.",listOf("Gorn mentions that Wolf wants to speak with you. Find Wolf in the New Camp.","Wolf teaches you how to remove minecrawler plates without charging learning points for the quest-specific need.","During the Free Mine retaking and exploration, kill minecrawlers and collect at least 15 plates.","Return to Wolf and give him the plates. He needs time to finish the armor.","Come back in Chapter V to collect the completed Crawler Plate Armour."),"About 3,000 XP; Crawler Plate Armour (collected in Chapter V)","",listOf("wolf","minecrawler plates","armor","free mine")),
        Quest("G1-C4-05",4,5,"Search for the ULU-MULU",listOf(),"Main","Ur-Shak / Tarrok","Old castle → Free Mine","Meet Ur-Shak and learn you need safe passage through Orc City","Help the orc slave Tarrok and collect four monster trophies so he can craft the ULU-MULU symbol of peace.",listOf("Ur-Shak explains that walking into Orc City as a human is suicide unless you carry an ULU-MULU, a respected sign that prevents ordinary orcs from attacking on sight.","Go to the Free Mine. Gomez’s men have taken it, so help Gorn and the New Camp fighters retake the mine as you descend.","Find Tarrok, the injured orc slave in the lower levels. Recover the medicine he needs and give it to him.","Tarrok teaches the trophy-harvesting skills required and asks for four components: a troll tusk, swamp shark teeth, a fire lizard/varan tongue and a shadowbeast horn.","Hunt the required creatures, collect the trophies and return to Tarrok. He crafts the ULU-MULU.","Optional: report the liberation of the Free Mine to Lee when the dialogue is available for an additional reward."),"Very large quest/combat XP; ULU-MULU","",listOf("ulu-mulu","tarrok","free mine","troll tusk","swamp shark","shadowbeast")),
        Quest("G1-C5-01",5,1,"Way into the Sleeper's Temple",listOf("Way to the Sleeper Temple"),"Main","Ur-Shak / story progression","Orc City → Sleeper Temple","Obtain the ULU-MULU","Use the ULU-MULU to cross Orc City, enter the Sleeper Temple and defeat the first four undead orc shamans.",listOf("Equip/carry the ULU-MULU and enter Orc City. Ordinary orcs treat the symbol as a sign of peace, so avoid attacking them if you want safe passage.","Open the temple route. Depending on the gate section, use the intended orc statue/telekinesis or teleport solution to bypass the sealed entrance.","Explore the vast temple carefully. Solve switches and traps, and defeat the first four undead shamans. Take each ancient blade they carry.","In Varrag-Ruuushk’s area, find and take the unusual sword that later proves to be URIZIEL.","Eventually encounter Grash-Varrag-Arushat, who cannot be harmed with ordinary weapons. Retreat rather than wasting resources.","Return to Xardas with the strange sword so he can identify a way to make it effective."),"","",listOf("sleeper temple","orc city","ulu-mulu","undead shamans","uriziel")),
        Quest("G1-C5-02",5,2,"The Magic Sword URIZIEL",listOf(),"Main","Xardas / Milten","Xardas’ tower → Sunken Tower → New Camp","Retrieve the strange sword from Sleeper Temple","Recover Xardas’ ancient armor, learn the charging formula and use the New Camp ore mound to restore URIZIEL’s power.",listOf("Bring the strange sword from the Sleeper Temple to Xardas. He identifies it as URIZIEL but explains that its magical power is exhausted.","Xardas sends you to the Sunken Tower. Explore it and recover the Ancient Ore Armor and the teleport rune/related items from his hidden cache.","Return to Xardas. He provides the formula or instructions needed to recharge URIZIEL.","Find Milten and bring him into the plan. Travel to the enormous ore mound controlled by the Water Mages in the New Camp.","Perform the ritual with Milten to channel the ore mound’s energy into URIZIEL. This destroys the Water Mages’ accumulated ore plan but restores the sword.","Return to Xardas. A magic-focused character may be able to convert the power into a rune instead of using URIZIEL purely as a sword.","With the charged weapon/rune, return to the Sleeper Temple and defeat Grash-Varrag-Arushat, the previously invulnerable fifth shaman."),"","",listOf("uriziel","xardas","milten","ore mound","ancient ore armor")),
        Quest("G1-C6-01",6,1,"The Awakening of the Sleeper",listOf("The Sleeper Awakens"),"Final main quest","Xardas / Cor Kalom","Deep Sleeper Temple","Charge URIZIEL and defeat the fifth undead shaman","Reach the Sleeper’s chamber, defeat Cor Kalom’s cultists and pierce the five heart shrines with the ancient orc blades.",listOf("Return to the Sleeper Temple with charged URIZIEL (or its rune equivalent) and defeat the final undead shaman who was previously invulnerable.","Push deeper through the temple until Xardas appears near the final altar area and explains the ritual required to banish the Sleeper.","Continue into Cor Kalom’s chamber. Defeat Kalom and the fanatical templars/novices protecting the Sleeper.","Use the five ancient blades taken from the undead shamans on the five heart shrines surrounding the final chamber.","After each heart is pierced, a demon lord appears behind you. Kill it before activating the next heart so the room does not become unmanageable.","Pierce the fifth heart. The Sleeper is banished and the Barrier collapses, ending Gothic."),"","Make a permanent save before the final descent.",listOf("sleeper","cor kalom","xardas","heart shrines","ancient blades"))
    )

    val chapter1 get() = quests.filter { it.chapter == 1 }.sortedBy { it.playOrder }
    fun chapter(number: Int) = quests.filter { it.chapter == number }.sortedBy { it.playOrder }
}
